#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"functions-api\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure Qiskit Functions access on an instance {#configure-qiskit-functions-access-on-an-instance}"
msgstr "Configurarea accesului la Qiskit Functions pe o instanță {#configure-qiskit-functions-access-on-an-instance}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use these instructions to configure Qiskit Functions access on an existing IBM Quantum Compute Service instance by using the IBM Cloud Resource Controller API.  Follow the instructions in order, as the commands build on each other.  For example, variables such as the token and URL are set in one step and reused in later steps. \n"
msgstr "Folosește aceste instrucțiuni pentru a configura accesul la Qiskit Functions pe o instanță IBM Quantum Compute Service existentă, utilizând API-ul IBM Cloud Resource Controller.  Urmează instrucțiunile în ordine, deoarece comenzile se bazează una pe cealaltă.  De exemplu, variabile precum tokenul și URL-ul sunt setate într-un pas și reutilizate în pașii următori. \n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prerequisites {#prerequisites}"
msgstr "Cerințe preliminare {#prerequisites}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An IBM Cloud API key (also called a token).  If necessary, create your API key on the [dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com). \n"
msgstr "O cheie API IBM Cloud (numită și token).  Dacă este necesar, creează-ți cheia API pe [dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com). \n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CRN of the instance you want to configure.  The instance's CRN is listed on your [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page.\n"
msgstr "CRN-ul instanței pe care vrei să o configurezi.  CRN-ul instanței este listat pe pagina ta de [Instanțe](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Get a bearer token {#step-1-get-a-bearer-token}"
msgstr "Pasul 1: Obținerea unui token bearer {#step-1-get-a-bearer-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exchange your API key for a bearer token. You will pass this token in the authorization header of all resource controller requests. Run the following code to generate a bearer token:\n"
msgstr "Schimbă-ți cheia API pentru un token bearer. Vei trece acest token în headerul de autorizare al tuturor cererilor către resource controller. Rulează următorul cod pentru a genera un token bearer:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request POST \\\n"
"  --url 'https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token' \\\n"
"  --header 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \\\n"
"  --data 'apikey=<YOUR_API_KEY>&grant_type=urn%3Aibm%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Aapikey'\n"
"  --silent | jq .\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"import requests\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "api_key = \"<YOUR_API_KEY>\"\n"
msgstr "api_key = \"<YOUR_API_KEY>\"\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.post(\n"
"    \"https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token\",\n"
"    headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"},\n"
"    params={\n"
"        \"apikey\": api_key,\n"
"        \"grant_type\": \"urn:ibm:params:oauth:grant-type:apikey\",\n"
"    },\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"token = resp.json()[\"access_token\"]\n"
"print(token) \n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.post(\n"
"    \"https://iam.cloud.ibm.com/identity/token\",\n"
"    headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"},\n"
"    params={\n"
"        \"apikey\": api_key,\n"
"        \"grant_type\": \"urn:ibm:params:oauth:grant-type:apikey\",\n"
"    },\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"token = resp.json()[\"access_token\"]\n"
"print(token) \n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The response includes an `access_token` field, which is your bearer token. Copy this value.\n"
msgstr "Răspunsul include un câmp `access_token`, care este tokenul tău bearer. Copiază această valoare.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Verify access {#step-2-verify-access}"
msgstr "Pasul 2: Verificarea accesului {#step-2-verify-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before making any changes, confirm that your token works and inspect the current instance configuration.\n"
msgstr "Înainte de a face orice modificare, confirmă că tokenul tău funcționează și inspectează configurația curentă a instanței.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"The CRN must be manually URL-encoded in the path. Replace each `:` with `%3A` and each `/` with `%2F`. For example, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` becomes `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"curl\" label=\"cURL\">\n"
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"CRN-ul trebuie codat URL manual în cale. Înlocuiește fiecare `:` cu `%3A` și fiecare `/` cu `%2F`. De exemplu, `crn:v1:bluemix:...` devine `crn%3Av1%3Abluemix%3A...`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"import urllib.parse\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"
msgstr "crn = \"<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>\"\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CRN will be URL-encoded into the path."
msgstr "CRN-ul va fi codat URL în cale."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"instance_url = (\n"
"    \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"    + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
")\n"
"headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\n"
msgstr ""
"instance_url = (\n"
"    \"https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/\"\n"
"    + urllib.parse.quote(crn, safe=\"\")\n"
")\n"
"headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"}\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(instance_url, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(instance_url, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `200 OK` response confirms that your token is valid. The current instance configuration is in the extensions field of the response. Use this instead of parameters, which might be stale.\n"
msgstr "Un răspuns `200 OK` confirmă că tokenul tău este valid. Configurația curentă a instanței se află în câmpul extensions al răspunsului. Folosește-l pe acesta în loc de parameters, care ar putea fi neactualizat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"step-3\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Look up the account-level functions configuration {#step-3-look-up-the-account-level-functions-configuration}"
msgstr "Pasul 3: Consultarea configurației funcțiilor la nivel de cont {#step-3-look-up-the-account-level-functions-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An instance can only be granted access to what the account is entitled to. Before configuring the instance, look up the account's configuration so you know which functions, business models, and permissions are available to grant. This is the source of truth for the values you will send in Step 4.\n"
msgstr "O instanță poate primi acces doar la ceea ce este autorizat contul. Înainte de a configura instanța, consultă configurația contului pentru a ști ce funcții, modele de afaceri și permisiuni sunt disponibile pentru a fi acordate. Aceasta este sursa de adevăr pentru valorile pe care le vei trimite la Pasul 4.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call `GET /accounts/{id}` on the Qiskit Runtime API with your API key. The `{id}` is your account ID without the `a/` prefix.  You can find it from the instance CRN (`crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...`).\n"
msgstr "Apelează `GET /accounts/{id}` pe API-ul Qiskit Runtime cu cheia ta API. `{id}` este ID-ul contului tău fără prefixul `a/`.  Îl poți găsi din CRN-ul instanței (`crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/<ACCOUNT_ID>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: apikey <YOUR_API_KEY>'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"account_id = \"<ACCOUNT_ID>\"  # from the CRN: crn:...:a/<ACCOUNT_ID>:...\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    f\"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/{account_id}\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\"},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"for plan in resp.json()[\"plans\"]:\n"
"    print(plan[\"plan_id\"], plan.get(\"functions\"), plan.get(\"custom_functions\"))\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.get(\n"
"    f\"https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/accounts/{account_id}\",\n"
"    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"apikey {api_key}\"},\n"
"    timeout=30,\n"
")\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"for plan in resp.json()[\"plans\"]:\n"
"    print(plan[\"plan_id\"], plan.get(\"functions\"), plan.get(\"custom_functions\"))\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each plan in the response includes a functions array and, if configured, a `custom_functions` object. These list the exact name, provider, business model, and permissions values you can grant to an instance under that plan.\n"
msgstr "Fiecare plan din răspuns include un array de funcții și, dacă este configurat, un obiect `custom_functions`. Acestea listează numele exact, furnizorul, modelul de afaceri și valorile de permisiuni pe care le poți acorda unei instanțe din acel plan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"`GET /accounts/{id}` shows what is available to grant at the account level. `GET /functions` (see [Verify the result](#verify-result)) shows what a specific instance has already been granted. Use the **account** endpoint to discover valid values, and the **functions** endpoint to confirm the result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Configure functions access {#step-4-configure-functions-access}"
msgstr "Pasul 4: Configurarea accesului la funcții {#step-4-configure-functions-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the instance to grant access to Catalog Functions and Custom Functions.\n"
msgstr "Actualizează instanța pentru a acorda acces la Catalog Functions și Custom Functions.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important notes\">\n"
"- The `name`, `provider`, and `business_model` values in functions must exactly match entries configured at the account level (see the [previous step](#step-3)). Permissions must be a non-empty subset of the account's permissions for that function. Similarly, `custom_functions.permissions` must be a non-empty subset of the account's `custom_functions` permissions.\n"
"- Include a timestamp in parameters on every PATCH. The Resource Controller deduplicates PATCH requests by comparing incoming parameters to the last value it stored. If they match, the request is silently dropped with `200 OK` without reaching the service. Include a changing timestamp value to prevent this.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note importante\">\n"
"- Valorile `name`, `provider` și `business_model` din functions trebuie să se potrivească exact cu intrările configurate la nivel de cont (vezi [pasul anterior](#step-3)). Permissions trebuie să fie un subset nevid al permisiunilor contului pentru acea funcție. În mod similar, `custom_functions.permissions` trebuie să fie un subset nevid al permisiunilor `custom_functions` ale contului.\n"
"- Include un timestamp în parameters la fiecare PATCH. Resource Controller elimină duplicatele cererilor PATCH comparând parametrii primiți cu ultima valoare stocată. Dacă se potrivesc, cererea este eliminată silențios cu `200 OK` fără a ajunge la serviciu. Include o valoare de timestamp în schimbare pentru a preveni acest lucru.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request PATCH \\\n"
"  --url 'https://resource-controller.cloud.ibm.com/v2/resource_instances/<YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN_URL_ENCODED>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_BEARER_TOKEN>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n"
"  --data '{\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"      \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:00Z\",\n"
"      \"functions\": [\n"
"        {\n"
"          \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"          \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"          \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"          \"permissions\": [\n"
"            \"function.read\",\n"
"            \"function.run\",\n"
"            \"function-files.read\",\n"
"            \"function-files.write\"\n"
"          ]\n"
"        }\n"
"      ],\n"
"      \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"        \"permissions\": [\n"
"          \"function-custom.write\",\n"
"          \"function-custom.run\"\n"
"        ]\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"  }'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"from datetime import datetime, timezone\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "A changing timestamp keeps the Resource Controller from de-duplicating the request."
msgstr "Un timestamp în schimbare împiedică Resource Controller să elimine duplicatele cererii."

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n"
"timestamp = _now.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{_now.microsecond:06d}000Z\"\n"
msgstr ""
"_now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n"
"timestamp = _now.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.\") + f\"{_now.microsecond:06d}000Z\"\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"body = {\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"        \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"        \"functions\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"                \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"                \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"                \"permissions\": [\n"
"                    \"function.read\",\n"
"                    \"function.run\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.read\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.write\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"            }\n"
"        ],\n"
"        \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"            \"permissions\": [\"function-custom.write\", \"function-custom.run\"],\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"body = {\n"
"    \"parameters\": {\n"
"        \"timestamp\": timestamp,\n"
"        \"functions\": [\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"name\": \"<FUNCTION_NAME>\",\n"
"                \"provider\": \"<PROVIDER>\",\n"
"                \"business_model\": \"<BUSINESS_MODEL>\",\n"
"                \"permissions\": [\n"
"                    \"function.read\",\n"
"                    \"function.run\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.read\",\n"
"                    \"function-files.write\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"            }\n"
"        ],\n"
"        \"custom_functions\": {\n"
"            \"permissions\": [\"function-custom.write\", \"function-custom.run\"],\n"
"        },\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"print(resp.json()[\"extensions\"])\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `200 OK` response indicates success. The updated configuration appears in the extensions field of the response.\n"
msgstr "Un răspuns `200 OK` indică succes. Configurația actualizată apare în câmpul extensions al răspunsului.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove functions access {#remove-functions-access}"
msgstr "Eliminarea accesului la funcții {#remove-functions-access}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Catalog Functions {#catalog-functions}"
msgstr "Catalog Functions {#catalog-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To remove Catalog Functions from an instance, send a PATCH with `\"functions\": null`:\n"
msgstr "Pentru a elimina Catalog Functions de la o instanță, trimite un PATCH cu `\"functions\": null`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"--data '{\n"
"  \"parameters\": {\n"
"    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:01Z\",\n"
"    \"functions\": null\n"
"  }\n"
"}'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"body = {\"parameters\": {\"timestamp\": timestamp, \"functions\": None}}\n"
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `\"functions\": []` (an empty array) equivalently clears Catalog Functions. `null` is the canonical form.\n"
msgstr "Setarea `\"functions\": []` (un array gol) elimină echivalent Catalog Functions. `null` este forma canonică.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom Functions {#custom-functions}"
msgstr "Custom Functions {#custom-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To remove Custom Functions from an instance, send a PATCH with `\"custom_functions\": null`:\n"
msgstr "Pentru a elimina Custom Functions de la o instanță, trimite un PATCH cu `\"custom_functions\": null`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"--data '{\n"
"  \"parameters\": {\n"
"    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-30T00:00:02Z\",\n"
"    \"custom_functions\": null\n"
"  }\n"
"}'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"body = {\"parameters\": {\"timestamp\": timestamp, \"custom_functions\": None}}\n"
"resp = requests.patch(instance_url, headers=headers, json=body, timeout=30)\n"
"resp.raise_for_status()\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `\"custom_functions\": {\"permissions\": []}` equivalently clears custom functions. `null` is the canonical form.\n"
msgstr "Setarea `\"custom_functions\": {\"permissions\": []}` elimină echivalent custom functions. `null` este forma canonică.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-result\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify the result {#verify-the-result}"
msgstr "Verificarea rezultatului {#verify-the-result}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To confirm that the instance has the correct Qiskit Functions configuration, use `GET /functions` from the Qiskit Runtime API instead of the Resource Controller. The Resource Controller's stored state might be stale if account-level changes updated the instance outside of the Resource Controller.\n"
msgstr "Pentru a confirma că instanța are configurația corectă de Qiskit Functions, folosește `GET /functions` din API-ul Qiskit Runtime în loc de Resource Controller. Starea stocată de Resource Controller ar putea fi neactualizată dacă modificările la nivel de cont au actualizat instanța în afara Resource Controller.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```bash\n"
"curl --request GET \\\n"
"  --url 'https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1/functions' \\\n"
"  --header 'Authorization: apikey <YOUR_API_KEY>' \\\n"
"  --header 'Service-CRN: <YOUR_INSTANCE_CRN>'\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    ```python\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Service-CRN header takes the raw CRN, not the URL-encoded form."
